@startuml
!include style.puml

title Fragmentation at the minimum MTU

participant "Transport L1" as TX $phoneFill
participant "GATT Server L1" as GS $pumpFill

autonumber

note over TX, GS
  ATT_MTU = 23, so 19 octets of
  fragment payload per write
end note

note over TX
  BOLUS_REQ PDU is 22 octets:
  8 header + 4 payload + 8 MAC + 2 CRC
end note

TX -> GS : write CMD, hdr 0x80 FIRST idx 0, 19 octets
note right of GS : FIRST resets the reassembly buffer
TX -> GS : write CMD, hdr 0x41 LAST idx 1, 3 octets
note right of GS : LAST completes, 22 octets passed to L2
GS ->> TX : BOLUS_RSP, fragmented the same way

note over TX, GS $noteBad
  The reassembly buffer is discarded on disconnection,
  on a FIRST arriving mid-message, on an index
  discontinuity, and above 512 octets. A buffer that
  survives a disconnection is how two unrelated messages
  get spliced into one valid-looking PDU. Hazard H-09.
end note

@enduml
